/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A heart sound is a short vibration from the heart and great vessels.
   - S1 is the first sound.
   - Most of the energy of S1 and S2 lies below about 200 Hz, and S3 and S4 sit at the very low end, below about 50 Hz.
   - A stethoscope has a chest piece, tubing and earpieces.
   - The bell is an open cup.
   - Tubing matters.
   - A phonocardiograph records the heart sound as a waveform.
   - The band-pass filter keeps the heart-sound band and rejects baseline wander below about 25 Hz and high-frequency noise above its upper cutoff.
   - A simultaneous ECG channel is the time reference.
*/
